<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Coligny</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1555">1555</a>–<a href="/years/1560">1560</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Coligny was the stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> Antarctique, built in 1555 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicolas-durand-de-villegaignon">Nicolas Durand de Villegaignon</a> on Serigipe island in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanabara-bay">Guanabara Bay</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, and named after Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaspard-de-coligny">Gaspard de Coligny</a>, the colony's patron. It sheltered French Catholics and Protestants allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tupinamba">Tupinambá</a>. The Portuguese governor-general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mem-de-sa">Mem de Sá</a> took and destroyed it in 1560.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-coligny.jpg" alt="Fort Coligny" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Forte-villegagnon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
